The Lamp
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/foundry]

FIXME(dread): When he turns toward you, the Color is the only part of him the lamp catches: his eyes, intense with it, the same purple beyond purple from the scrub now burning behind a living face. Out in the glare it never registered. Here it is unmistakable.

choices:

* Ask who he is = Press him on the standing he carries [requires !tag foundry.asked_who]
    FIXME(mundane): He allows that he is someone, or was. He was brothers with most of the men who run the Kesharat now; rode with them, got into the kind of trouble young men get into, in the good years when they were all young together. "A long time ago. They chose a different path." He still likes trouble. He just does it alone now. Nothing about "a long time ago" fits the young face saying it, and he offers nothing to fix the discrepancy.
    +add_tag foundry.asked_who
    +open "The Lamp"

* Ask how he walked past the guards = Your ring failed; he never broke stride [requires !tag foundry.asked_guards]
    FIXME(dread): Kesharat privilege, he calls it. "I don't take much interest in the Lattice, but the thing takes a keen interest in me. It clears obstables from my way. Like those guards."
    +add_tag foundry.asked_guards
    +open "The Lamp"

* Go deeper into the factory = Follow his lamp-less ease into the dark
    FIXME(dread): The corridor gives out onto the open floor of the place, and the lamp finds no walls. The dark speaks from three directions at once.
    +open "The Factory Floor"
